#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114992 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "51a437bf-2a11-5eba-a046-4770d41214ca" :question/math-academy-id "e-4720" :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/38c4cba166fdfcd0954a18156946e41834a626cccee4baab976861dd23574c85.png) Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the identity matrix and replacing the second row with the result of adding $5$ times the first row to the second row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=5{R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation $R_2:=5R_1+ R_2$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114993 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/id #uuid "9927d1a6-a119-5987-9f49-5171a3f2e2d3" :question/math-academy-id "e-4721" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation $R_1:=R_1 - R_2$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA\\mathbin{:}$\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/a4a2b1035b3b5699ff3558ffa839fbd667ad6defaf30a158d628c7011ab97aa8.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114994 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/id #uuid "0f08f8aa-63e3-500a-987e-e9888b9b0479" :question/math-academy-id "e-4722" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nR_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2, \\qquad  R_2:=R_2+3R_1\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is $R_1 \\leftrightarrow R_2.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is $R_2:=R_2+3R_1.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by $E_1$ on the left and get $E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/d35cb368b7380f08e486757813138fa3f3332ed40a9b0e5faeab7a20c3119bef.png)\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to $E_1 A,$ we multiply by $E_2$ on the left and get $E_2 E_1 A\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14058391/assets/c87dbe6c81a670dd62d8a130d3085b2e9b36d5d3ad27d53bda571ec69b639689.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335952 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e1005add-fabb-5f0a-ac68-14bd4d203cac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335954} {:answer/id #uuid "ace3e252-598c-5764-b4de-1cf96054b120" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-5{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335955} {:answer/id #uuid "ba81e26c-dc38-5105-9f61-e6d3752b58a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335956} {:answer/id #uuid "95c0daf0-5855-5be4-bc60-e829b6b6ef61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+5{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335957} {:answer/id #uuid "056ef133-5828-5d46-bcfa-f500220c80c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+(-5){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e1005add-fabb-5f0a-ac68-14bd4d203cac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335954} :answer-field/id #uuid "8c579582-ba2c-5ec1-a1e7-b2a4e1ae5469" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c25477cb-b615-5c8d-82e5-e31fcd78f3c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-130838" :question/problem "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The matrix $E$ is obtained by taking the second row of the identity matrix and adding $-5$ times the first row:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b73cd82-0f02-5dc7-a807-9e2c9ed55874" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-10{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335961} {:answer/id #uuid "b4a0467f-ff99-5c0c-a11f-4e98a6ad2917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{1}+(-10){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335962} {:answer/id #uuid "fe0ce350-4910-5a63-920d-6dd23ab2711d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-10{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335963} {:answer/id #uuid "4311829c-f7a9-5a69-b836-9d15e71fdec6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-10){R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335964} {:answer/id #uuid "20964ba5-e064-5ebb-9140-cc139adeb3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=10{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe0ce350-4910-5a63-920d-6dd23ab2711d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{2}:=-10{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335963} :answer-field/id #uuid "984622ea-54b6-5c74-b57c-3a458d3c24dc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e513b774-583b-518a-8b52-207376a2ba3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-130839" :question/problem "Let $E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -10\\end{aligned}].$ Find the row operation that, when applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A,$ gives the result of the product $EA.$" :question/worked-solution "The given matrix $E$ is obtained by multiplying the second row of the identity matrix by $-10$: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=-10{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $EA$ is equivalent to applying the row operation  ${R}_{2}:=-10{R}_{2}$ to $A.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186335966 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f47800-98b3-512e-af20-1899e6b0c86d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Row Operation That's Equivalent To Left Multiplication by an Elementary Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff9d1f1c-ee0e-5dd3-9866-ce20b3a783d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-8){R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335968} {:answer/id #uuid "0a729055-e8ce-5aa7-8e3f-a4a057648160" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:=8{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335969} {:answer/id #uuid "8da60480-bb57-5d52-bdc6-67450243f1f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+8{R}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186335970} {:answer/id #uu