e given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-15){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -15 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336001 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "94c2cd65-810b-52ad-a20d-7b5a0a9eaf2b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Given Row Operation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "005f69de-eb91-59b5-bf38-fbad0306dcc8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336003} {:answer/id #uuid "5949911c-9c93-52cb-99d7-1e63d4ef58e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 18\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336004} {:answer/id #uuid "453e9062-dfba-55fa-a0e2-3afbe42e23d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & -18 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336005} {:answer/id #uuid "94f340e1-e695-530e-8a05-07280a75e2ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -18 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336006} {:answer/id #uuid "610adf77-3d0b-5624-97b5-8e6d3353935c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336007}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "610adf77-3d0b-5624-97b5-8e6d3353935c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336007} :answer-field/id #uuid "f6d7be51-09ed-59ce-952e-c48aae7c1d3c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336002}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0d67f596-0dbd-5c8b-92a9-8470a352853f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130853" :question/problem "Suppose we are applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=18{R}_{1}$ to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ Find the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "We need to find an elementary matrix $E$ such that $EA$ is equivalent to applying the elementary row operation ${R}_{1}:=18{R}_{1}$ to $A.$\n\nTo find $E,$ we apply the given row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=18{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =E\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication is $EA:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336008 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f56dc83b-7ea5-5749-9837-625c25b62458" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336010} {:answer/id #uuid "ec77a1c5-8162-5571-a04f-52f407983473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336011} {:answer/id #uuid "84624887-a6cb-5e14-b4cb-0ee763449a5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336012} {:answer/id #uuid "a58fb034-4cb3-57bf-b446-74b89d96a1cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336013} {:answer/id #uuid "2ec3976c-0e3c-5d5c-879a-5913152ea249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2ec3976c-0e3c-5d5c-879a-5913152ea249" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336014} :answer-field/id #uuid "c42acb86-0d07-56db-80ec-8fc5caabdcd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "15dd603e-a758-58d8-860b-2ef6fc62e3fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-130859" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations.\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1}.$ The corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row  operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1}:=6{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336015 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2042ae33-bf4f-5854-8d8e-58303a8516a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336017} {:answer/id #uuid "88017268-1873-5440-b4f1-c96f2471b10c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336018} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc0d89c-debb-54e3-bd19-047956d61a9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336019} {:answer/id #uuid "fc0adcf7-4b1b-5613-ad6c-f8587b2562dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336020} {:answer/id #uuid "72b1c920-40d6-5526-ba27-ec72faa7a5fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336021}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2042ae33-bf4f-5854-8d8e-58303a8516a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336017} :answer-field/id #uuid "c358645d-a11a-5b3f-abb4-a16433a437da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f834b7b-a5bd-54ad-b193-00aa4b7d256c" :question/math-academy-id "q-130860" :question/problem "Suppose that the following elementary row operations, in the given order, are to be applied to a $2\\times 2$ matrix $A:$\n\n$$\n{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1},\\,{R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}\n$$\n\nFind the equivalent notation in terms of matrix multiplication." :question/worked-solution "First, let's find the elementary matrices corresponding to the two given elementary row operations\n\n- The first elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}.$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- The second elementary row operation is ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2}$ The  corresponding elementary matrix can be found by applying this same elementary row operation to the identity matrix as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{5}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={E}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo apply the first elementary row operation to the matrix $A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{1}$ on the left and get ${E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$\n\nThen, to apply the second elementary row operation to ${E}_{1}A,$ we multiply by ${E}_{2}$ on the left and get ${E}_{2}{E}_{1}A:$ \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186336022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c6f890b-fab1-51f1-9ac7-b680553c835a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Matrix Product That's Equivalent To a Sequence of Row Operations"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65e05b66-f640-58d4-8e66-2ee28d523684" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336024} {:answer/id #uuid "b8240825-fa88-5391-a4c1-aa8a57eefc0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\cdot A" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336025} {:answer/id #uuid "4eae1f52-3206-5706-a988-3604efb036d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\be